1
00:00:03,191 --> 00:00:11,991
Configure your clinic — Settings ▸ Practice — The settings everything else inherits — identity, hours, and the rules scheduling follows.

2
00:00:17,301 --> 00:00:22,908
Settings ▸ Clinic Settings is the clinic’s identity — and almost every other screen reads from it.

3
00:00:22,908 --> 00:00:31,986
The name, address and phone print on invoices and statements, and show on the public booking page.

4
00:00:31,986 --> 00:00:39,732
Tax ID and NPI are what claims are submitted under — a claim with the wrong NPI comes straight back.

5
00:00:39,732 --> 00:00:55,461
Currency is set once here and every price, quote and invoice in the system follows it.

6
00:00:55,461 --> 00:01:00,892
Working Hours is the outer boundary of the whole calendar: nothing can be booked outside it.

7
00:01:00,892 --> 00:01:11,614
Each day has its own open and close, and its own switch — late clinic on Thursday, half day Saturday, closed Sunday.

8
00:01:11,614 --> 00:01:28,408
A day switched off is greyed out. Providers can still be given narrower hours of their own inside this.

9
00:01:28,408 --> 00:01:31,862
Appointment Settings is where the calendar gets its shape.

10
00:01:31,862 --> 00:01:40,041
Default duration is the length a new appointment starts at. Slot interval is the grid the day is cut into.

11
00:01:40,041 --> 00:01:46,889
Maximum advance booking caps how far ahead a patient can book — set it to the horizon you can actually staff.

12
00:01:46,889 --> 00:01:57,674
And the cancellation deadline is the cut-off the patient sees when they try to cancel late.

13
00:01:57,674 --> 00:02:03,312
Three screens, ten minutes — and the calendar, the booking page and the claims all behave.

14
00:02:03,404 --> 00:02:16,424
What you just did

15
00:02:17,051 --> 00:02:26,051
Health | Efficiency | Growth — More in the Getting Started series — the next video is linked on screen.
